workspace_library.py:168 inserts the notice at body[1] only while `self.message` is set. The message is cleared and the page re-rendered when an Add starts (:584, :598), set at the end (:629, :634), and set by Remove (:681), Read again (:710) and the backup tick (set_travels, :718-726).

Flet's frozen diff (flet/controls/object_patch.py, `build_keys`: unkeyed controls are matched by their position among unkeyed siblings) pairs body children by position. In-memory `ObjectPatch.from_diff` of the page structure, built with the real workspace_components:
- same structure (Enter in the search field): search field identity kept (True);
- an Add finishes and the first message appears: search field False, question field False;
- an Add starts and the message is cleared: False, False;
- backup box ticked on a fresh page: checkbox False, search field False;
- the same trees with explicit keys on the three cards: True.

workspace_shell.py:500-503 promises that focus and caret survive a re-render. STAGE37_RAG §1.1 says a document is indexed while the page searches, so typing during an Add is intended use.

workspace_library.py:918 builds the caption from `source.location`, and library_ask.location (:140-147) is English by design because it goes into the prompt. In-memory render of LibraryPage._answer:
- ru: '[S1] Вымышленный обзор · page 2 · Копинг как медиатор · DABCDEF12-p2.1', while T['library.page'] in RU is 'стр. 2';
- lv: the same 'page 2', while LV is '2. lappuse';
- `location()` without page or section gives 'start of the document'.

locale_audit cannot see runtime strings like these, so its missing count stays 0.

In memory, `ai_assist.unverified_quotes(reply, 'Mann-Whitney U test. synth_stress by synth_group: U = 120.0, p = 0.031, r = 0.34.')` gives:
- 'Тест «Манна–Уитни» показал различие (p = 0.031).' → ['Манна–Уитни'];
- 'Mann–Whitney testa („neparametriskais tests“) rezultāts' → ['neparametriskais tests'];
- 'The "Mann–Whitney U test" found p = 0.031.' → [].

workspace_assistant.py:145 sends `language=app.session.language`, and describe_result labels plus the engine report are English. library_ask.py:65 has 'Quote a source only word for word, inside quotation marks.' ai_assist.RULES (:46-56) and TASK_RULES have no such rule. The gate's mocked replies contain no quotes, so tests/test_stage368_ai_gate.py stays green.
